{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>These are the words.</b> Since they are words of reproof, he enumerates here all the places where they provoked the Omnipresent in them — therefore he obscured the words and recalled them by allusion, for the honor of Israel (see Sifrei)." "<b>To all Israel.</b> If he had reproved only some of them, those in the market would say: You were listening from the son of Amram and you answered nothing — such and such? Had we been there we would have answered him! Therefore he gathered them all and said to them: Behold, you are all here; whoever has a reply, let him reply (Sifrei)." "<b>In the wilderness.</b> They were not in the wilderness but in the plains of Moab. So what is 'in the wilderness'? Rather, on account of that by which they provoked Him in the wilderness, when they said (Exodus 16) ״מִי יִתֵּן מוּתֵנוּ״ and so forth." "<b>In the Aravah.</b> On account of the Aravah — that they sinned with Baal Peor at Shittim in the plains of Moab." "<b>Opposite Suf.</b> On account of that they rebelled at the Sea of Suf when they came to the Sea of Suf, when they said (Exodus 14) ״הֲמִבְּלִי אֵין קְבָרִים בְּמִצְרַיִם״, and likewise when they journeyed from within the sea, as it says (Psalms 106) ״וַיַּמְרוּ עַל יָם בְּיַם סוּף״, as is in Arakhin (15a)." "<b>Between Paran and between Tophel and Laban.</b> Rabbi Yochanan said: We searched all of Scripture and found no place whose name is Tophel and Laban. Rather, he reproved them concerning the matters that were תָּפְלוּ over the מָן, which is לָבָן, as they said (Numbers 21) ״וְנַפְשֵׁנוּ קָצָה בַּלֶּחֶם הַקְּלֹקֵל״, and concerning what they did in the wilderness of Paran through the spies." "<b>And Hazeroth.</b> At the rebellion of Korah. Another interpretation: he said to them — you should have learned from what I did to Miriam at Hazeroth on account of evil speech, yet you spoke in that place." "<b>And Di Zahav.</b> He reproved them concerning the calf that they made because of the abundance of gold they had, as stated (Hosea 2) ״וְכֶסֶף הִרְבֵּיתִי לָהּ וְזָהָב עָשׂוּ לַבָּעַל״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:28.156781446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}